# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Added to address the "Trust and Safety" section of PageSpeed Insights'
# Best Practices audit: CSP against XSS, HSTS, COOP (clickjacking/origin
# isolation), and X-Frame-Options.
#
# ⚠️ IMPORTANT: the Content-Security-Policy allowlist below was built by
# scanning every external domain referenced in the current source code
# (Google Fonts, Sanity, the wsrv.nl image proxy, social share links, the
# Worker API, etc). It has NOT been verified against a live build in a
# browser — please deploy to a preview URL first and click through the
# whole site (including the admin dashboard, image uploads, and any embeds)
# with devtools' Console open before pointing production traffic at it. Any
# domain the console reports as blocked just needs adding to the relevant
# directive below.
#
# ⚠️ MONETAG TRADE-OFF (deliberate, revisit later): connect-src and img-src
# below are opened to all HTTPS origins (`https:`) because Monetag's ad
# scripts (In-Page Push, zone 11383412) call constantly-rotating tracking
# domains (my.rtmark.net, jhnwr.com, 3leap.com, ispvh.com, dawac.com, ...)
# that change without notice — allow-listing them one by one was not
# sustainable. This means a successful XSS on this site could exfiltrate
# data to any HTTPS endpoint and load any HTTPS image — script-src is
# still locked down to specific domains, so arbitrary *script* injection
# via CSP bypass is not opened up, only data/image egress. Once ad revenue
# is stable and AdSense is re-applied for, consider tightening this back
# down (e.g. dropping Monetag, or re-scoping to a specific ad vendor CDN
# if they publish one).
#
# Note: Google's legacy "ads/ga-audiences" remarketing pixel fires against
# the visitor's local Google ccTLD (google.com.tw, google.co.uk, google.de,
# ...) which is impossible to whitelist exhaustively in img-src without
# effectively opening it to all of google.*. It's a Google Ads audience-
# building pixel, not required for GA4 reporting itself — if it keeps
# showing as a blocked console error, turn off "Remarketing"/"Ads Personalization"
# under the GA4 property's Google Signals / Ads Linking settings instead of
# widening the CSP for it.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://nap5k.com https://tzegilo.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https:; frame-src 'self' https://www.facebook.com https://nap5k.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
